{
  "mn43:0.1": "Middle Discourses 43 ",
  "mn43:0.2": "The Great Elaboration ",
  "mn43:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn43:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn43:1.3": "Then in the late afternoon, Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita came out of retreat, went to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn43:1.4": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "mn43:2.1": "“Reverend, they speak of ‘a witless person’. ",
  "mn43:2.2": "How is a witless person defined?” ",
  "mn43:2.3": "“Reverend, they’re called witless because they don’t understand. ",
  "mn43:2.4": "And what don’t they understand? ",
  "mn43:2.5": "They don’t understand: ‘This is suffering’ … ‘This is the origin of suffering’ … ‘This is the cessation of suffering’ … ‘This is the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering.’ ",
  "mn43:2.6": "They’re called witless because they don’t understand.” ",
  "mn43:2.7": "Saying “Good, reverend,” Mahākoṭṭhita approved and agreed with what Sāriputta said. Then he asked another question: ",
  "mn43:3.1": "“They speak of ‘a wise person’. ",
  "mn43:3.2": "How is a wise person defined?” ",
  "mn43:3.3": "“They’re called wise because they understand. ",
  "mn43:3.4": "And what do they understand? ",
  "mn43:3.5": "They understand: ‘This is suffering’ … ‘This is the origin o